33	/**
34	 *
35	 *
36	 * Functional guide to example:
37	 *
38	 * - EmacPsErrorHandler() demonstrates how to manage asynchronous
39	 *errors.
40	 *
41	 * - EmacPsResetDevice() demonstrates how to reset the driver/HW
42	 *without loosing all configuration settings.
43	 *
44	 *
45	 * <pre>
46	 * MODIFICATION HISTORY:
47	 *
48	 * Ver   Who  Date     Changes
49	 * ----- ---- --------
50	 *------------------------------------------------------- 1.00a wsy
51	 *01/10/10 First release 1.00a asa  11/25/11 The cache disable
52	 *routines are removed. So now both I-cache and D-cache are
53	 *enabled. The array RxBuffer is removed to avoid an extra copy
54	 *from RxBuffer to RxFrame. Now the address of RxFrame is submitted
55	 *to the Rx BD instead of the address of RxBuffer. In function
56	 *EmacPsDmaSingleFrameIntrExample, BdRxPtr is made as a pointer
57	 *instead of array of pointers. This is done since on the Rx path
58	 *we now submit a single BD instead of all 32 BDs. Because of this
59	 *change, relevant changes are made throughout the function
60	 *		      EmacPsDmaSingleFrameIntrExample.
61	 *		      Cache invalidation is now being done for the RxFrame
62	 *		      buffer.
63	 *		      The unnecessary cache flush (Xil_DCacheFlushRange) is
64	 *		      removed. This was being done towards the end of the
65	 *		      example which was unnecessary.
66	 * 1.00a asa 01/24/12  Support for Zynq board is added. The SLCR
67	 *divisors are different for Zynq. Changes are made for the same.
68	 * 		      Presently the SLCR GEM clock divisors are hard-coded
69	 *		      assuming that IO PLL output frequency is 1000 MHz.
70	 * 		      The BDs are allocated at the address 0xFF00000 and
71	 *the 1 MB address range starting from this address is made
72	 * 		      uncached. This is because, for GEM the BDs need to be
73	 * 		      placed in uncached memory. The RX BDs are allocated
74	 *at address 0xFF00000 and TX BDs are allocated at address
75	 * 		      0xFF10000.
76	 * 		      The MDIO divisor used of 224 is used for Zynq board.
77	 * 1.01a asa 02/27/12  The hardcoded SLCR divisors for Zynq are
78	 *removed. The divisors are obtained from xparameters.h.c. The
79	 *sleep values are reduced for Zynq. One sleep is added after MDIO
80	 *divisor is set. Some of the prints are removed. 1.01a asa
81	 *03/14/12  The SLCR divisor support for ENET1 is added. 1.01a asa
82	 *04/15/12  The funcation calls to Xil_DisableMMU and Xil_EnableMMU
83	 *		      are removed for setting the translation table
84	 *		      attributes for the BD memory region.
85	 * 1.05a asa 09/22/13 Cache handling is changed to fix an issue
86	 *(CR#663885). The cache invalidation of the Rx frame is now moved
87	 *to XEmacPsRecvHandler so that invalidation happens after the
88	 *			  received data is available in the memory. The
89	 *variable TxFrameLength is now made global. 2.1	srt 07/11/14
90	 *Implemented 64-bit changes and modified as per Zynq Ultrascale Mp
91	 *GEM specification 3.0  kpc  01/23/14 Removed PEEP board related
92	 *code 3.0  hk   03/18/15 Added support for jumbo frames. Add cache
93	 *flush after BD terminate entries. 3.2  hk   10/15/15 Added clock
94	 *control using CRL_APB_GEM_REF_CTRL register. Enabled 1G speed for
95	 *ZynqMP GEM. Select GEM interrupt based on instance present.
96	 *                    Manage differences between emulation platform
97	 *and silicon. 3.2  mus  20/02/16.Added support for INTC interrupt
98	 *controlller. Added support to access zynq emacps interrupt from
99	 *                    microblaze.
100	 * 3.3 kpc   12/09/16 Fixed issue when -O2 is enabled
101	 * 3.4 ms    01/23/17 Modified xil_printf statement in main
102	 *function to ensure that "Successfully ran" and "Failed" strings
103	 *                   are available in all examples. This is a fix
104	 *for CR-965028. 3.5 hk    08/14/17 Dont perform data cache
105	 *operations when CCI is enabled on ZynqMP. 3.8 hk    10/01/18 Fix
106	 *warning for redefinition of interrupt number. 3.9 hk    02/12/19
107	 *Change MDC divisor for Versal emulation. 03/06/19 Fix BD space
108	 *assignment and its memory attributes. 03/20/19 Fix alignment
109	 *pragmas for IAR compiler.
110	 *
111	 * </pre>
112	 *
113	 *****************************************************************************/
